<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <%- include('partials/head') %>
  <title>Analyze Recording · <%= companyName %></title>
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('partials/adminnav') %>

  <main class="wide">
    <div class="page-head">
      <div>
        <h1>Analyze Recording</h1>
        <p>Audit calls that happened outside the platform — upload the audio and get the same transcript, checklist, and flags as a live call.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <p class="muted">
        Did the welcome call happen outside the platform (e.g. your PM called and recorded it on his phone)?
        Upload the recording here (.mp3, .m4a, .wav — up to 25MB), pick which client it belongs to, and the AI will
        transcribe it, audit it against the welcome-call script, run the full flag checklist —
        including <strong>anything the caller said that goes outside the script</strong> — and attach the recording,
        transcript, and results to the client's record just like a live call.
      </p>
      <% if (!hasKey) { %>
        <div class="alert alert-error">
          <%- include('partials/icon', { name: 'alert', size: 16 }) %>
          <div>
            <strong>One-time setup needed:</strong> this feature uses OpenAI for transcription and auditing.
            Create an API key at platform.openai.com → API keys, then add it in Railway → Variables as
            <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code>. A few dollars of credit covers many hours of audio.
          </div>
        </div>
      <% } %>
      <% if (error) { %><div class="alert alert-error"><%- include('partials/icon', { name: 'alert', size: 16 }) %><div><%= error %></div></div><% } %>
      <form method="post" action="/admin/analyze" enctype="multipart/form-data" class="stack" id="analyze-form">
        <label>Which client is this recording for?
          <select name="call_id" id="client-select" required>
            <option value="auto" selected>Auto-detect from the recording (recommended)</option>
            <option value="new">New client — enter details manually</option>
            <% calls.forEach((c) => { %>
              <option value="<%= c.id %>"><%= c.homeowner_name %> · <%= c.phone %> (<%= c.status.replace('_',' ') %>)</option>
            <% }) %>
          </select>
        </label>
        <div id="new-client-fields" class="hidden">
          <div class="grid-form">
            <label>Full name <span class="req">*</span><input name="new_name" maxlength="200"></label>
            <label>Phone <span class="req">*</span><input name="new_phone" maxlength="40" type="tel"></label>
            <label>Property address <span class="req">*</span><input name="new_address" maxlength="400"></label>
            <label>Email<input name="new_email" type="email" maxlength="200"></label>
            <label>Installer<input name="new_installer" maxlength="200"></label>
            <label>Account
              <select name="new_script_variant">
                <option value="old">Old</option>
                <option value="new" selected>New</option>
              </select>
            </label>
          </div>
          <p class="fineprint">A client record is created automatically and the recording, transcript, and audit are attached to it.</p>
        </div>
        <script>
          const clientSelect = document.getElementById('client-select');
          const newFields = document.getElementById('new-client-fields');
          clientSelect.addEventListener('change', () => {
            const isNew = clientSelect.value === 'new';
            newFields.classList.toggle('hidden', !isNew);
            ['new_name', 'new_phone', 'new_address'].forEach((n) => {
              document.querySelector(`[name="${n}"]`).required = isNew;
            });
          });
        </script>
        <label>Recording file
          <input type="file" name="audio" accept=".mp3,.m4a,.wav,.aac,.ogg,audio/*" required>
        </label>
        <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit" id="analyze-btn" <%= hasKey ? '' : 'disabled' %>><%- include('partials/icon', { name: 'search', size: 15 }) %> Transcribe &amp; audit recording</button>
        <div class="alert alert-success hidden" id="analyze-progress" role="status">
          <%- include('partials/icon', { name: 'audio', size: 16 }) %>
          <div><strong>Working on it…</strong> Uploading, transcribing, and auditing the recording. This takes 30–90 seconds — please keep this page open. You'll be taken to the client's record when it finishes.</div>
        </div>
        <p class="fineprint">
          Auto-detect listens for the name, address, and phone number the homeowner states during the call,
          matches them against your client list, and attaches the audit to that record — or creates a new
          record if nobody matches. Pick a client manually any time the recording is unclear.
          Processing takes 30–90 seconds; you'll land on the client's record with the results.
        </p>
      </form>
    </div>
  </main>
<script>
    document.getElementById('analyze-form').addEventListener('submit', () => {
      setTimeout(() => {
        const btn = document.getElementById('analyze-btn');
        btn.disabled = true;
        btn.textContent = 'Working — transcribing & auditing…';
        document.getElementById('analyze-progress').classList.remove('hidden');
      }, 0);
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
